120: the same conifold replacement on both sides. The
121: identification extends over \(D^3\times S^2\), with
122: its transported meridian and Hopf Euler line. The
123: remaining exterior is a product bordism. Therefore
124: the difference of the two completed Jin six-manifolds
125: is the relative collision boundary of \(W_{\rm rel}\),
126: with the parameter-convention sign in IE.5.
127: This cancels actual selected scalar traces; it does
128: not supply a holomorphic full selected corner.
129: 
130: ## IE.3. The E doubles and actual Cartier class
131: 
132: The marked source small resolution in the unit
133: Weierstrass coordinates of IF.5 is
134: \[
135:  A=Dz,\quad C=Bz,\quad X=Bz,\quad
136:  Y=(B+Dz)/2,\quad v_0=(B-Dz)/2 .
137: \]
138: At \(v_0=0\) the I2 has components \(C_0,C_1\);
139: the marked section meets \(C_1\), and \(O\) meets
140: \(C_0\). The actual degree-two section closure has
141: Cartier equation
142: \[
143:                   1-Bz^3-(1-2v_0)z^2=0 .
144: \]
145: It restricts to \(C_0\) with multiplicity one and
146: does not contain \(C_1\). Consequently
147: \[
148:  c_1(M_1)[C_1]=1,\qquad c_1(M_2)[C_1]=2.               \tag{IE.3}
149: \]
150: The second equality retains the actual vertical
151: Cartier specialization \(2G-O=C_0\).
152: 
153: The local source patch retracts onto its I2
154: plumbing: use the radial collapse of \(xy=t\)
155: to the axes in the two node charts and the
156: component normal-disc retractions elsewhere.
157: Its integral two-cycle lattice has primitive
158: basis \(F=C_0+C_1,C_1\), with pairing
159: \[
160:                   \begin{pmatrix}0&0\\0&-2\end{pmatrix}.       \tag{IE.4}
161: \]
162: The normalized component two-cells give integral
163: \(C_0,C_1\), and the zero-section relative disc
164: meets \(F\) once. The smooth source resolution
165: is a submersion over \(v_0\), also with boundary,
166: so this marking transports to \(S_{\epsilon_*}\).
167: 
168: On the reference chain (IE.1) the positive normal
169: line is literally \(M_a\), and the negative one
170: is \(M_a^{-1}\). Conjugating the negative-weight
171: line gives determinant
172: \[
173:                           b_{\rm r}=2c_1(M_a).          \tag{IE.5}
174: \]
175: It evaluates to zero on \(F\) and \(2a\) on \(C_1\).
176: Its boundary class is zero integrally: in the
177: central Tate marking \(QP^2=1\), so \(Z^aV^2\)
178: is a nonvanishing boundary frame. Transport that
179: actual frame through the smooth source/Cartier
180: family. Equivalently the boundary component class
181: has order two and (IE.5) kills it. A relative lift
182: is \(-aC_1\), up to the null fibre and a boundary
183: connecting class. Thus
184: \[
185:                               b_{\rm r}^2=-2a^2.        \tag{IE.6}
186: \]
187: 
188: The collision E patch is identified with the
189: same minimal I2 patch by the source character
190: \(Z\), base coordinate \(t\), and primitive
191: source-period stabilizer. Its two star rays
192: have height one, so there is no extra base
193: ramification or exceptional curve. The actual
194: normal determinant is marked by
195: \[
196:                          Z^aV^2/\xi_E^{\,2j+1}.
197: \]
198: The dual-character order is zero on both
199: components. Hence in this boundary marking
200: \[
201:                                b_{\rm c}^2=0.           \tag{IE.7}
202: \]
203: Replacing \(\xi_E=\epsilon/t\) by \(\epsilon\)
204: adds the explicit boundary gauge \(t^{2j+1}\).
205: It may be odd and is retained. A boundary
206: gauge changes the glued class by the
207: Mayer--Vietoris image of \(H^1(\partial S;\mathbb Z)\).
208: Its square and its product with the glued
209: determinant class vanish. Indeed represent
210: the connecting class as \(d\chi\wedge\alpha\)
211: in the collar; its square repeats \(d\chi\),
212: and its product integrates the zero boundary
213: restriction of the other class. Thus the
214: actual derivative of (IE.2) has exactly the
215: square difference (IE.7) minus (IE.6).
216: 
217: The source patches are oriented diffeomorphic
218: with boundary. Their closed double has
219: signature zero and hence tangent Pontryagin
220: integral zero. This uses only the ordinary
221: four-dimensional fixed-surface signature
222: identity. With weights \(+1,-1\), its
223: normal-link contribution is
224: \[
225:  \frac1{24}\int_{S_{\rm c}\cup(-S_{\rm r})}
226:             \{p_1(TS)-3b^2\}=-\frac{a^2}{4}.           \tag{IE.8}
227: \]
228: There are exactly \(N\) E doubles: the actual
229: scalar period shifts the primitive chain by
230: \(N\), and the collision-boundary source
231: loop fixes these labels.
232: 
233: ## IE.4. Finite stabilizers and the actual Stokes identity
234: 
235: Remove invariant normal tubes of every fixed
236: component from \(W_{\rm rel}\). The physical
237: circle is locally free on the complement.
238: Its quotient is a compact oriented
239: seven-dimensional orbifold \(Z\), carrying
240: the actual orbifold Euler line with class \(x\).
241: 
242: A slice with stabilizer \(\mu_d\) gives a
243: finite chart \(\widetilde U/\mu_d\). Average
244: metrics, partitions of unity and connections
245: over \(\mu_d\) and over the physical circle.
246: Normalize the connection by
247: \(\alpha(\delta)=1\). Its curvature represents
248: the same physical \(x\) on every chart. The
249: actual tangent splitting is
250: \[
